---
# Starlight's <Tabs> (user-components/Tabs.astro): {% tabs sync: "aspire-lang" %}{% tab "C#", icon: "seti:c-sharp" %}...{% endtab %}{% endtabs %}.
#
# DEVIATION from Starlight: Starlight renders the tab list on the server from the panels (rehype-tabs). A shortcode
# renders its body first and cannot see its children as data, so here each {% tab %} renders
# `<div role="tabpanel" data-label="..." data-icon="...">` and this shortcode renders an EMPTY
# `<div class="tablist-wrapper not-content"><ul role="tablist"></ul></div>`. The client script (scripts/client, the
# `starlight-tabs` element) fills the list from the DIRECT `[role=tabpanel]` children before Starlight's own logic
# runs, giving the same final DOM as Starlight:
#   <starlight-tabs data-sync-key><div class="tablist-wrapper not-content"><ul role="tablist">
#     <li role="presentation" class="tab"><a role="tab" href="#tab-panel-N" id="tab-N" aria-selected tabindex>[svg] label</a></li>...
#   </ul></div><div id="tab-panel-N" aria-labelledby="tab-N" role="tabpanel" [hidden]>...</div>...<starlight-tabs-restore>
# and restores the synced tab (localStorage `starlight-synced-tabs__<sync>`). Until it runs, the CSS rule in
# assets/css/shortcodes-extra.css shows only the first panel. `<starlight-tabs-restore>` is emitted as Starlight does
# (last child, synced tabs only); its inline definition script is replaced by the client element's restore logic.
# Root class: cid-sl-tabs.
block: true
params: [sync]
---
<starlight-tabs class="cid-sl-tabs"{% if sync %} data-sync-key="{{ sync | escape }}"{% endif %}><div class="tablist-wrapper not-content"><ul role="tablist"></ul></div>{{ body | strip }}{% if sync %}<starlight-tabs-restore></starlight-tabs-restore>{% endif %}</starlight-tabs>